  "reason": "Existing evidence shows that RNA-only models with scvi_n200 encoder (config_005: 0.6501 accuracy) outperform multimodal setups using the same RNA encoder but resnet50 images (config_030: 0.6315 accuracy). This experiment tests whether replacing resnet50 with a more complex imagenet_vit_l image encoder in a multimodal multiprofile setup (with scvi_n200 RNA, avgpool aggregation, and concat fusion) can bridge this performance gap. It isolates the effect of image encoder complexity while maintaining consistent RNA encoding and aggregation strategies, addressing uncertainty about the role of advanced image encoders in multimodal performance."
